{"probes":[{"id":"vault-raft-contract","summary":"Live checks confirmed an independent node1 Vault instance and a three-voter, unsealed Raft cluster on node2-node4. Versioned KV proof and cross-endpoint evaluator operations succeeded; evaluator data was removed during cleanup.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["Two initial node1 commands had evaluator shell-quoting errors before a corrected status/configuration command succeeded.","Node1 protected mount enumeration was unavailable because no protected root token file was discovered; the role was established from independent Shamir/file status and the Raft members' live Transit seal configuration/status."]},{"id":"vault-raft-operational-state","summary":"Services, processes, listeners, protected paths, residue, mounts, auth, audit, policies, and snapshots were inspected read-only. A wildcard infraset-admin policy remains.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["Transit seal-token lookup/capability inspection returned seal_token_lookup_failed; the token was not printed, so its exact ACL could not be independently confirmed."]}],"assertions":[{"id":"vault-raft-required-topology","status":"pass","summary":"node1 is initialized, unsealed, Shamir-sealed, file-backed, and independent. Nodes2-node4 report the same Transit-sealed Raft cluster, are initialized and unsealed, and the live peer configuration has exactly three voters with node2 as the sole leader.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n sh -c '\ncfg=/etc/vault.d/vault.hcl\naddr=$(grep api_addr \"$cfg\" | head -1 | cut -d \\\" -f2)\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-status===\"\nVAULT_ADDR=\"$addr\" VAULT_CACERT=/etc/vault/pki/ca.crt vault status -format=json\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===config-shape===\"\ngrep -HnE \"^[[:space:]]*(api_addr|cluster_addr|storage[[:space:]]+|seal[[:space:]]+|path[[:space:]]*=|address[[:space:]]*=|mount_path[[:space:]]*=|key_name[[:space:]]*=|tls_(cert|key|client_ca_file)|tls_disable)\" \"$cfg\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===listeners===\"\nss -tlnp 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"vault|:8200|:8201\" || true\n'","observation":"Vault status: type=shamir, initialized=true, sealed=false, storage_type=file, ha_enabled=false. Configuration uses file storage and node1 TLS cert/key with the shared CA; the Vault service listens on its API and cluster listeners."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c '\n. /root/vault-admin.env\nexport VAULT_CACERT=/etc/vault/pki/ca.crt\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===status===\"\nvault status -format=json\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===raft-peers===\"\nvault operator raft list-peers -format=json\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===autopilot===\"\nvault operator raft autopilot state -format=json\n'","observation":"Status: type=transit, initialized=true, sealed=false, storage_type=raft, ha_enabled=true. Raft peers contain exactly node2, node3, and node4, all voter=true; node2 is the only leader. Autopilot Healthy=true, FailureTolerance=1, Voters=[node2,node3,node4], NonVoters=null."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c '\n. /root/vault-admin.env\nexport VAULT_CACERT=/etc/vault/pki/ca.crt\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===status===\"\nvault status -format=json\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===raft-peers===\"\nvault operator raft list-peers -format=json\n'","observation":"Status reports the same initialized, unsealed Transit/Raft cluster as node2. The peer list independently shows node2 as sole leader and node2-node4 as the three voters."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c '\n. /root/vault-admin.env\nexport VAULT_CACERT=/etc/vault/pki/ca.crt\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===status===\"\nvault status -format=json\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===raft-peers===\"\nvault operator raft list-peers -format=json\n'","observation":"Status reports the same initialized, unsealed Transit/Raft cluster as node2. The peer list independently shows node2 as sole leader and node2-node4 as the three voters."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The initial malformed node1 commands were corrected before the successful evidence above."]},{"id":"vault-raft-kv-service","status":"pass","summary":"The required proof secret is readable, secret/ is KV version 2, and a unique versioned evaluator value was written on node2, read consistently on node3 and node4, then deleted.","evidence":[{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c '\n. /root/vault-admin.env\nexport VAULT_CACERT=/etc/vault/pki/ca.crt\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===proof===\"\nvault kv get -field=proof secret/infraset\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===secret-engine=[REDACTED] secrets list -format=json\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===admin-file-mode===\"\nstat -c \"%a %U:%G\" /root/vault-admin.env\n'","observation":"proof=raft-auto-unseal. secret/ is type=kv with options.version=2. /root/vault-admin.env is mode 600 root:root."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c '\n. /root/vault-admin.env\nexport VAULT_CACERT=/etc/vault/pki/ca.crt\np=secret/infraset-eval-20260826-155518-jomvway\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===write===\"\nif vault kv put \"$p\" proof=raft-auto-unseal-eval-155518 revision=1; then printf \"%s\\n\" put_ok; else printf \"%s\\n\" put_failed; fi\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===read===\"\nvault kv get -format=json \"$p\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===metadata===\"\nvault kv metadata get -format=json \"$p\"\n'","observation":"Write returned put_ok; read returned both evaluator fields with metadata version=1; metadata current_version=1."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c '\n. /root/vault-admin.env\nexport VAULT_CACERT=/etc/vault/pki/ca.crt\np=secret/infraset-eval-20260826-155518-jomvway\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===proof===\"\nvault kv get -field=proof secret/infraset\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===cross-endpoint-read===\"\nvault kv get -format=json \"$p\"\n'","observation":"proof=raft-auto-unseal. The unique value was readable through node3 with the same fields and version=1."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c '\n. /root/vault-admin.env\nexport VAULT_CACERT=/etc/vault/pki/ca.crt\np=secret/infraset-eval-20260826-155518-jomvway\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===cross-endpoint-read===\"\nvault kv get -format=json \"$p\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===delete===\"\nvault kv delete \"$p\"\n'","observation":"The unique value was readable through node4 with version=1; delete returned Success! Data deleted."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["A cleanup-side exit-status check on node2 reported the soft-deleted path as present; node3 then destroyed evaluator version 1 and node4 confirmed the evaluator proof field was absent."]},{"id":"vault-raft-state-clean","status":"fail","summary":"No failed units, duplicate Vault processes, debug listeners, snapshots, stale installers, or unprotected key/admin files were observed. However, the live infraset-admin ACL grants wildcard access with broad capabilities, which is concrete overbroad policy state.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n sh -c '\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===failed-units===\"\nsystemctl --failed --no-legend --plain || true\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-processes===\"\nps -C vault -o user=,pid=,ppid=,comm=\nprintf \"vault_process_count=%s\\n\" \"$(pgrep -x vault | wc -l)\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-unit-shape===\"\nsystemctl show vault --property=ExecStart,ActiveState,SubState,EnvironmentFiles --no-pager\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-config-and-pki-modes===\"\nfind /etc/vault /etc/vault.d -maxdepth 3 -type f -printf \"%m %u:%g %p\\n\" 2>/dev/null | head -120\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===sensitive-named-files-modes===\"\nfind /var/lib/vault /root /tmp /var/tmp /opt /usr/local/src -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -iname \"*vault*\" -o -iname \"*token*\" -o -iname \"*recovery*\" -o -iname \"*.key\" -o -iname \"*.pem\" -o -iname \"*.snap\" -o -iname \"*.snapshot\" -o -iname \"*.tar*\" -o -iname \"*.deb\" -o -iname \"*.rpm\" \\) -printf \"%m %u:%g %p\\n\" 2>/dev/null | head -200\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===tcp-listeners===\"\nss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | head -100\n'","observation":"No failed units; exactly one vault process; Vault service active. Node1 CA/cert are 644 root:vault, private key 640 root:vault, root-held transit init/token files are 600 root:root, and no snapshot/temp/archive residue was listed. Only expected Vault API/cluster listeners appeared."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n sh -c '\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===failed-units===\"\nsystemctl --failed --no-legend --plain || true\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-processes===\"\nps -C vault -o user=,pid=,ppid=,comm=\nprintf \"vault_process_count=%s\\n\" \"$(pgrep -x vault | wc -l)\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-config-shape-redacted===\"\ngrep -HnE \"^[[:space:]]*(api_addr|cluster_addr|storage[[:space:]]+|seal[[:space:]]+|path[[:space:]]*=|address[[:space:]]*=|mount_path[[:space:]]*=|key_name[[:space:]]*=|token[[:space:]]*=|tls_)\" /etc/vault.d/vault.hcl 2>/dev/null | sed -E \"s/(token[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*).*/\\1<redacted>/\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===protected-path-modes===\"\nstat -c \"%a %U:%G %n\" /root/vault-admin.env /etc/vault/pki/ca.crt /etc/vault/pki/*.crt /etc/vault/pki/*.key /etc/vault.d/vault.hcl /etc/vault.d/vault.env 2>/dev/null\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===sensitive-named-files-modes===\"\nfind /var/lib/vault /root /tmp /var/tmp /opt /usr/local/src -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -iname \"*vault*\" -o -iname \"*token*\" -o -iname \"*recovery*\" -o -iname \"*.key\" -o -iname \"*.pem\" -o -iname \"*.snap\" -o -iname \"*.snapshot\" -o -iname \"*.tar*\" -o -iname \"*.deb\" -o -iname \"*.rpm\" \\) -printf \"%m %u:%g %p\\n\" 2>/dev/null | head -200\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===tcp-listeners===\"\nss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | head -100\n'","observation":"No failed units; exactly one vault process; expected Transit/Raft/TLS configuration; /root/vault-admin.env is 600 root:root, Vault DB is 600 vault:vault, node private key is 640 root:vault, and no snapshot/temp/archive residue was listed. Only expected Vault API/cluster listeners appeared."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n sh -c '\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===failed-units===\"\nsystemctl --failed --no-legend --plain || true\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-processes===\"\nps -C vault -o user=,pid=,ppid=,comm=\nprintf \"vault_process_count=%s\\n\" \"$(pgrep -x vault | wc -l)\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-config-shape-redacted===\"\ngrep -HnE \"^[[:space:]]*(api_addr|cluster_addr|storage[[:space:]]+|seal[[:space:]]+|path[[:space:]]*=|address[[:space:]]*=|mount_path[[:space:]]*=|key_name[[:space:]]*=|token[[:space:]]*=|tls_)\" /etc/vault.d/vault.hcl 2>/dev/null | sed -E \"s/(token[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*).*/\\1<redacted>/\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===protected-path-modes===\"\nstat -c \"%a %U:%G %n\" /root/vault-admin.env /etc/vault/pki/ca.crt /etc/vault/pki/*.crt /etc/vault/pki/*.key /etc/vault.d/vault.hcl /etc/vault.d/vault.env 2>/dev/null\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===sensitive-named-files-modes===\"\nfind /var/lib/vault /root /tmp /var/tmp /opt /usr/local/src -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -iname \"*vault*\" -o -iname \"*token*\" -o -iname \"*recovery*\" -o -iname \"*.key\" -o -iname \"*.pem\" -o -iname \"*.snap\" -o -iname \"*.snapshot\" -o -iname \"*.tar*\" -o -iname \"*.deb\" -o -iname \"*.rpm\" \\) -printf \"%m %u:%g %p\\n\" 2>/dev/null | head -200\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===tcp-listeners===\"\nss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | head -100\n'","observation":"No failed units; exactly one vault process; expected Transit/Raft/TLS configuration; /root/vault-admin.env is 600 root:root, Vault DB is 600 vault:vault, node private key is 640 root:vault, and no snapshot/temp/archive residue was listed. Only expected Vault API/cluster listeners appeared."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n sh -c '\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===failed-units===\"\nsystemctl --failed --no-legend --plain || true\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-processes===\"\nps -C vault -o user=,pid=,ppid=,comm=\nprintf \"vault_process_count=%s\\n\" \"$(pgrep -x vault | wc -l)\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===vault-config-shape-redacted===\"\ngrep -HnE \"^[[:space:]]*(api_addr|cluster_addr|storage[[:space:]]+|seal[[:space:]]+|path[[:space:]]*=|address[[:space:]]*=|mount_path[[:space:]]*=|key_name[[:space:]]*=|token[[:space:]]*=|tls_)\" /etc/vault.d/vault.hcl 2>/dev/null | sed -E \"s/(token[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*).*/\\1<redacted>/\"\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===protected-path-modes===\"\nstat -c \"%a %U:%G %n\" /root/vault-admin.env /etc/vault/pki/ca.crt /etc/vault/pki/*.crt /etc/vault/pki/*.key /etc/vault.d/vault.hcl /etc/vault.d/vault.env 2>/dev/null\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===sensitive-named-files-modes===\"\nfind /var/lib/vault /root /tmp /var/tmp /opt /usr/local/src -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -iname \"*vault*\" -o -iname \"*token*\" -o -iname \"*recovery*\" -o -iname \"*.key\" -o -iname \"*.pem\" -o -iname \"*.snap\" -o -iname \"*.snapshot\" -o -iname \"*.tar*\" -o -iname \"*.deb\" -o -iname \"*.rpm\" \\) -printf \"%m %u:%g %p\\n\" 2>/dev/null | head -200\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===tcp-listeners===\"\nss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | head -100\n'","observation":"No failed units; exactly one vault process; expected Transit/Raft/TLS configuration; /root/vault-admin.env is 600 root:root, Vault DB is 600 vault:vault, node private key is 640 root:vault, and no snapshot/temp/archive residue was listed. Only expected Vault API/cluster listeners appeared."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c '\n. /root/vault-admin.env\nexport VAULT_CACERT=/etc/vault/pki/ca.crt\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===audit-devices===\"\nvault audit list -format=json\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===auth-methods===\"\nvault auth list -format=json\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===policies-and-rules===\"\nfor pol in $(vault policy list | tail -n +3); do\n  printf \"policy=%s\\n\" \"$pol\"\n  vault policy read \"$pol\" 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"^[[:space:]]*(path|capabilities)\" || true\ndone\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===transit-seal-token-capabilities=[REDACTED] \"^[[:space:]]*token[[:space:]]*=\" \"$cfg\" | head -1 | cut -d \\\" -f2)\nmount=$(grep \"^[[:space:]]*mount_path[[:space:]]*=\" \"$cfg\" | head -1 | cut -d \\\" -f2)\nkey=$(grep \"^[[:space:]]*key_name[[:space:]]*=\" \"$cfg\" | head -1 | cut -d \\\" -f2)\nmount=$(printf \"%s\" \"$mount\" | sed \"s:/*$::\")\nif [ -n \"$seal_token\" ] && [ -n \"$mount\" ] && [ -n \"$key\" ]; then\n  lookup=$(VAULT_TOKEN=[REDACTED] vault token lookup -format=json 2>/dev/null)\n  if [ -n \"$lookup\" ]; then\n    printf \"%s\\n\" \"$lookup\" | grep -E \"\\\"(policies|path|type|orphan)\\\"\" || true\n  else\n    printf \"%s\\n\" seal_token_lookup_failed\n  fi\n  for path in \"$mount/encrypt/$key\" \"$mount/decrypt/$key\" \"$mount/keys/$key\"; do\n    printf \"capabilities_path=%s\\n\" \"$path\"\n    VAULT_TOKEN=[REDACTED] vault token capabilities \"$path\" 2>/dev/null || true\n  done\nelse\n  printf \"%s\\n\" seal_token_or_live_seal_config_not_parseable\nfi\nprintf \"%s\\n\" \"===snapshot-and-temp-residue===\"\nfind /var/lib/vault /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -iname \"*.snap\" -o -iname \"*.snapshot\" -o -iname \"*executor*\" -o -iname \"*infraset*\" -o -iname \"*vault*.tar*\" -o -iname \"*vault*.deb\" -o -iname \"*vault*.rpm\" \\) -printf \"%m %u:%g %p\\n\" 2>/dev/null\n'","observation":"Audit list is empty; only the built-in token auth method is mounted. Policy inspection found infraset-admin with path \"*\" and capabilities create, read, update, delete, list, sudo. No snapshot, executor, infraset, or stale Vault installer residue was listed. Seal-token lookup returned seal_token_lookup_failed."}],"failures":["The live infraset-admin policy grants wildcard path access with create/read/update/delete/list/sudo capabilities, which is concrete overbroad policy state."],"limitations":["The seal-token capability loop produced no capability result after seal_token_lookup_failed; the token remained protected and was not printed."]}],"actions_performed":["Executed all authored Probe 1 evidence commands in order.","Created, read, deleted, and destroyed only the evaluator-owned KV path secret/infraset-eval-20260826-155518-jomvway.","Confirmed the evaluator data field was absent after cleanup and left all four Vault services active.","Executed all authored Probe 2 read-only inspection commands.","Called complete_evidence exactly once after all probes and cleanup."],"overall_summary":"Topology and versioned KV assertions pass. Operational-state assertion fails because infraset-admin retains a wildcard full-capability ACL; evaluator-created KV data was cleaned up and live evidence collection is closed."}
